Some folklore: they say that a grand new shiny machine translation
(English-Russian-English) was finished and was to be demonstrated to an
important official who incidentally didn't speak Russian.

So they fed the phrase "Out of sight, out of mind" into the system.
History forgot what the Russian result was, but they fed the result back
into the system so that the important guy could read it too. The second,
English result was "Invisible idiot".

